# Test grouping of .o inputs on conflicting -D defines:
# - Multiple .o files sharing the same conflicting define value (including
#   generated .c sources) are grouped into a single cc_library_static.
# - Objects without the conflicting define stay in the parent module without
#   inheriting any conflicting define, even when listed after conflicting .o files.
# - Generated sources and headers are attributed only to the group that owns them.
# - External shared_libs propagate from linking consumers to split group modules.
# - Non-conflicting optional defines (single value + unset) do not trigger splits.
src/libapp.so
src/libno_split.a
